    "notes": [
      {
        "moduleIds": [
          2
        ],
        "content": "## Intake insurance claims from email and portal submissions with Claude\n\nClaims teams that re-key first notice of loss from emails, forms and call notes.\n\n### How it works\nTrigger: Emails to claims@, portal and app submissions via webhook, and call-centre transcripts from the telephony platform.\n1. Capture the notice\n2. Extract the facts\n3. Verify policy and coverage\n4. Triage severity and complexity\n5. Screen fraud indicators\n6. Route\n7. Acknowledge the claimant\n8. Create the file and assign\nEvery AI step is followed by a \"Needs a person?\" gate that parks low-confidence items.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open \"Config (edit me)\" and fill in the fields (names, approver, quiet hours, thresholds).\n2. Add credentials: Anthropic, plus Claims system (Guidewire ClaimCenter, Duck Creek, Snapsheet, in-house), Policy admin, Telephony (Five9, Talkdesk).\n3. Run once with test_mode on, read the output, then switch the trigger on.\n\n### Customization tips\nDefine the claim types and the required documents in the Config node; point the write-back at your claims system.\nGuardrail to keep: Coverage determinations and claim decisions are made by adjusters; the workflow verifies and summarises.\n\nFull blueprint: https://agentmelt.com/workflows/insurance-claims-intake/",
        "isFilterNote": false,
        "metadata": {
          "color": "#F5D451"
        }
      }
    ],
    "zone": "eu1.make.com"
  }
}